  "prefLabel": "Ins 1501.10 Acquisition of Persons Controlling a Domestic Insurer",
  "priorExpiration": "2007-05-01",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Ins 1501.10 Acquisition of Persons Controlling a Domestic Insurer.\n\n(a) If the person being acquired is deemed to be a \"domestic insurer\" solely because of the provisions of RSA 401-B:3, I(d), the name of the domestic insurer on the cover page should be indicated as follows:\n\n“ ”, a subsidiary of\n\n(Insert name of insurance company)\n\n“ ”\n\n(Insert name of corporation)\n\n(b) Where a RSA 401-B:3, I(d) insurer is being acquired, references to \"the insurer\" contained in Form A shall refer to both the domestic subsidiary insurer and the person being acquired.\n\nSource. #1900, eff 1-1-82; ss by #4287, eff 7-1-87; ss by #5652, eff 7-1-93; ss by #6985, eff 5-1-99, EXPIRED: 5-1-07\n\nNew. #8910, eff 7-1-07, eff 7-1-07; ss by #10450, eff 1-1-14; ss by #13692, eff 7-21-23",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/ins1500.html"
